---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="resume -- alexander campos" description="Alexander Campos - builds and ships agent memory and model routing, grounded in six years of regulated finance operations. Reframed (live), ForgeFrame (open source).">
  <article class="resume">
    <header class="masthead">
      <h1>Alexander Campos</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Banking operations · process, controls &amp; automation</p>
      <p class="contact-line">
        Washington D.C. Metro Area <span aria-hidden="true">|</span>
        <a href="mailto:alex@campos.works">alex@campos.works</a> <span aria-hidden="true">|</span>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/alexander-d-campos">linkedin.com/in/alexander-d-campos</a> <span aria-hidden="true">|</span>
        <a href="https://campos.works">campos.works</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <ul class="stats" aria-label="At a glance">
      <li><b>6 yrs</b><span>regulated finance ops</span></li>
      <li><b>~80</b><span>people, SOP governance</span></li>
      <li><b>$600M+</b><span>regulatory network monitored</span></li>
      <li><b>78%</b><span>less manual review</span></li>
      <li><b>20,000+</b><span>account failure resolved solo</span></li>
      <li><b>$35B</b><span>merger, zero transmission errors</span></li>
      <li><b>50+ hrs</b><span>cut in one quarter</span></li>
    </ul>

    <section class="summary">
      <p>
        Six years in regulated bank operations, promoted four times in five years from a
        teller line to owning SOP governance and controls for an ~80-person department.
        Built the failure-driven monitoring behind a $600M+ regulatory network (78% less
        manual), resolved a 20,000-account logic failure solo, and drove zero transmission
        errors through a $35B merger integration. I build controls to multinational and
        national regulatory standards, and the automation that runs them without a person
        in the loop -- removing the work rather than staffing it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Experience</h2>

      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div class="role-top">
            <h3 class="org">Capital One</h3>
            <span class="dates">Richmond, VA · June 2025 – Present</span>
          </div>
          <p class="title">Senior Process Manager, Card Legal Recoveries Operations</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Own the department's SOP governance function</strong> -- ~80 people
            across 8-9 teams. L5 SOP library, annual audits to the process-doc standard,
            ownership mapping, version history, and artifact change auditing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Stood up new controls and processes from the ground up</strong> to
            multinational and national regulatory standards across several regulatory
            bodies. Built with Engineering and the Data team, who validated each solution
            before it went live.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Run the controls loop on a $600M+ regulatory file-exchange network</strong>
            (300+ daily transmissions). Took anomaly detection from a rapid prototype to an
            automated pipeline, cutting manual monitoring 78% and turning every anomaly
            population into an identified control gap and a reconciled fix.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Built an automated business-review pipeline</strong> spanning six teams
            and 20+ operational data points. Consolidates into executive one-pagers that give
            senior leadership a noise-free read on what matters and why. It runs autonomously.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cut 50+ hours of manual work in a single quarter</strong> -- scripted
            automation across controls, process, monitoring, and analytics tasks.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Resolved a 20,000+ account logic failure</strong> independently while the
            Data team was backlogged 6+ weeks. Built an investigative SQL framework, isolated
            root cause, remediated, documented the failure taxonomy, and stood up monitoring
            on the surfaces it exposed.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Drove zero transmission errors through the $35B Discover merger
            integration.</strong> Serve as an AI subject-matter expert for the line of
            business and led the department's first governed AI adoption -- validated
            instruction sets, judgment and controls stayed human. Mentor management
            development program associates.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div class="role-top">
            <h3 class="org">Apple Federal Credit Union</h3>
            <span class="dates">Fairfax &amp; Lake Ridge, VA · January 2020 – May 2025</span>
          </div>
          <p class="title">Branch Operations Administrator</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Promoted four times in five years</strong> -- teller, consumer lending,
            branch operations, then enterprise support across 25 branches during a major
            merger. Completed bachelor's degree concurrently.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Architected a branch-wide modernization roadmap</strong> and presented it
            to the CEO with VP and SVP backing -- an end-to-end automation strategy for manual
            workflows across the branch network. Approved and moved into implementation.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Built compliance tracking and reporting infrastructure</strong> --
            Power BI, NCUA/CFPB documentation. Cut complaint response cycles 50%.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div class="role-top">
            <h3 class="org">Independent engineering</h3>
            <span class="dates">2025 – Present</span>
          </div>
          <p class="title">Shipped and running · campos.works</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Model evaluation</strong> -- paid adversarial eval design for
            frontier-model benchmarking in finance. I write cases where the plausible
            answer is wrong for a defensible reason, weight the rubric so cosmetic
            success does not pass, and trace a failed score back to the specific
            reasoning step that caused it rather than counting failed rows.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong><a href="https://reframed.works">Reframed</a></strong> -- the antithesis
            of AI-slop resumes and algorithmic rejection. Analysis platform shipped solo in
            22 days, live in production on multi-provider model routing. 76 API routes as of
            Aug 2026, Stripe billing, Neon Postgres.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Model routing engine</strong> -- tier-based dispatch with fallback chains,
            so a provider outage degrades instead of failing. Cut inference cost 40-60% in
            production, and runs under every project on the machine.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@forgeframe/server">ForgeFrame</a></strong>
            -- memory for agents, MIT licensed and published to npm. Strengthens with use,
            decays with neglect, constitutional memories never change. 888 tests (884 passing
            as of Aug 2026), 4 packages, live in production.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Client work</strong> -- bilingual proposal and invoicing tools for a
            landscaping company, running on his books today. Field notes in, a clean
            bilingual PDF out.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Skills</h2>

      <h3>Operations</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        SOP governance &amp; audits · Process modernization · Controls design ·
        Failure-surface monitoring · Dependency sequencing &amp; approval gates ·
        Metrics, KPIs &amp; executive reporting · Workflow automation · Change control ·
        Vendor operations
      </p>

      <h3>Regulated Environments</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        BSA/AML/KYC · SCRA · TILA/Reg Z · FDCPA/Reg F · NCUA · CFPB ·
        Systems integration &amp; onboarding
      </p>

      <h3>AI</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        Adversarial eval design &amp; red-teaming · Eval automation (weighted rubrics,
        failure-mode diagnosis) · Local open-source model benchmarking (Ollama, llama.cpp) ·
        Multi-provider model routing with fallback chains · Agent memory (MCP) ·
        Prompt &amp; instruction-set validation · Governed AI adoption in a regulated line of business
      </p>

      <h3>Data</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        SQL (Postgres, Snowflake) · Python · Splunk · Observe · Looker · Power BI · Tableau
      </p>

      <h3>Development</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        TypeScript · React · Node.js · Next.js · Astro · Electron · SQLite ·
        Python (Pandas, scikit-learn)
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Education &amp; certifications</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>B.S. Business Administration, Management and Operations</strong> -- George Mason
        University, December 2024.
      </p>
      <p class="skills">
        AI Governance Professional (AIGP, IAPP) -- in progress ·
        Business Process Management (2024) · Google Data Analytics (2024)
      </p>
    </section>

  </article>

  <script is:inline>
    console.log(
      '%c same question, different shapes. ',
      'color: #5BF29B; font-family: monospace; font-size: 11px;'
    );
  </script>
</Page>

<style>
  .resume {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .skills {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--white-60);
  }

  .role {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .role-header {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .role-header h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }

  .dates {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--white-45);
  }

  .role ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .role li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .role li strong {
    color: var(--glow-hot);
  }

  .resume-contact {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .resume-contact p {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--white-45);
  }
  .stats {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--white-15); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--white-15);
  }
  .stats li {
    padding: 0.85rem 0.5rem; text-align: center;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--white-08);
  }
  .stats li:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .stats b {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.55rem; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1;
    color: var(--glow-hot); letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .stats span {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--white-45); line-height: 1.35;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } .stats li:nth-child(4) { border-right: none; } }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } .stats li { border-right: none; } }

  /* ── The PDF's grammar, carried over ──
     Centered masthead, gold small-caps section rules, company in gold with
     place and dates on the right, italic title, tight bullets with bold leads.
     The stat strip is the one thing the paper version does not have. */
  .resume { font-size: 0.93rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .masthead { text-align: center; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .masthead h1 { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.04em; margin: 0 0 0.3rem; }
  .subtitle { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold-accent); margin: 0 0 0.55rem; }
  .contact-line { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--white-45); margin: 0; }
  .contact-line a { color: var(--white-60); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--white-15); }
  .contact-line a:hover { color: var(--gold-accent); border-bottom-color: var(--gold-accent); }
  .contact-line span { color: var(--white-15); margin: 0 0.4rem; }

  .resume .summary p { color: var(--white-70); max-width: 72ch; margin: 0; }
  .resume hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--white-08); margin: 1.6rem 0; }

  .resume h2 {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold-accent); font-weight: 500; margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gold-accent); opacity: 0.95;
  }
  .resume .role { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .resume .role-header { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }
  .role-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .resume .org { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.12rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--gold-accent); margin: 0; }
  .resume .dates { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--white-45); white-space: nowrap; }
  .resume .title { font-style: italic; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--white-60); margin: 0.1rem 0 0; }
  .resume .role ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
  .resume .role li { margin: 0 0 0.45rem; color: var(--white-70); }
  .resume .role li strong { color: var(--glow-hot); font-weight: 600; }
  .resume .role li a { color: var(--glow-hot); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--white-15); text-decoration: none; }

  .resume h3:not(.org) { font-family: var(--body); font-size: 0.86rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--glow-hot); margin: 0.7rem 0 0.2rem; }
  .resume .skills { font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .masthead h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
    .resume .dates { white-space: normal; }
    .contact-line span { display: none; }
    .contact-line a { display: block; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
  }
</style>
